    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-Harrisburg/Part-Time---Physics---Adjunct-Lecturer_REQ_0000080026-2": {
      "title": "Part Time - Physics - Adjunct Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants .   JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS Penn State Harrisburg’s School of Science, Engineering, and Technology invites applications for a part-time faculty opening in Physics, Astronomy, and/or Earth Science effective August 2026 .  Job Duties The successful candidate is expected to teach undergraduate Physics, Astronomy, and/or Earth Science courses.   Requirements and Qualifications Minimum qualifications include Master’s degree(s), at least one of which should be in physics or a closely related field, and relevant experience.  Applicants should submit a cover letter and resume at the time of application. Applicants will be reviewed based on their background, experience and educational credentials. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the vacancies are filled . Applicants should submit a web application, cover letter and resume.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Se